{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/951382-ephemeral-beings-influence-how-does-it-work","id":951382,"title":"Ephemeral beings' Influence ; How does it work?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-15T16:59:06-07:00","id":951382,"title":"Ephemeral beings' Influence ; How does it work?","content":"I've been playing CofD for ages now it seems. But our group have for the most part played Requiem and Ephemeral beings ain't a big deal there. And the ones I've used sure has had some interesting Influence purview but I've never really used them. The vagueness if what they are capable off is just a bit too arbitrary in my mind. But now we've started a mage chronicle and ephemeral beings are way more important in Mage then in Vampire. And one of my players is portraying an Thyrsus Shaman and another is portraying a Mastigos Psychonaut. Though they are not capable of summoning spirits or goetia yet, it will come. So i need to get a better understanding of what you can actually do with influence, both in a broad sense but also in a more defined sense with practical examples. I don't want to be a arbitrary judge at the gaming table so some rules consistency would help here.<br /> <br /> So to help you out, here comes some examples of Influences spirits in my chronicle have, but im not sure actually what they can do.<br /> <br /> Influence: Comradery 2<br /> <br /> Influence: Wisdom 3<br /> <br /> Influence: justice 2<br /> <br /> Influence: Fairness 2<br /> <br /> Influence: Cold 5 <br /> <br /> Influence: indoctrination 3<br /> <br /> <br /> So for example what can you concretely do with these? And how &quot;much&quot; would you gain so to speak. Mages spells have potency for example if you want to increase a skill roll with +2, thats a potency 2 spell. What would be the equivalence of potency for Influence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T17:57:24-07:00","id":951407,"title":"","content":"Have you looked at the chart on pg. 256? Influence 1 can act like Perfecting, Compelling, Unveiling and Knowing, Influence 2 is basically like Ruling, Influence 3 is like Weaving and Patterning, Influence 4 is like Making and Influence 5 is like Making with Advanced Scale and the option to make effects Lasting. Obviously, ephemeral entities have no respect for the actual Practices, but combining the descriptions of how Practices function with the description of Influences might give you some help. One thing to note, ephemeral entities have no ability to reduce or destroy things that fall under the purview of their Influence. That would run entirely contrary to their nature after all. That's how I try to grok it anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T18:25:43-07:00","id":951418,"title":"","content":"Yes the chart is my mortal enemy :P<br /> It talk about what each dot of influence is capable of doing but doesn't really go into what it does mechanically speaking except for ephemeral conditions and resonance and giving Structure or Health equal to rank.<br /> How much defense can i get? What are the rules for playing with emotions? Can i switch out virtues? Give or add dots in skills? attributes? merits? etc? If a room is a bit cold , can i Control it with Cold Influence 3 to create an extreme environment? At what level? Can i give out Conditions to PCs or NPCs in their area of Influence? <br /> <br /> Like i get a general understanding of what you can do with the Influence, but how do I go from concept into mechanical effects without arbitrary pulling stuff ex rectum. <br /> <br /> Take for instance Strengthen, one use of it is to give someone under its purview extra Defense. There is a lot of difference between +1, +1 per success and + rank or anything else.<br /> <br /> I just have a problem going from abstracts to mechanics in this case.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T18:57:30-07:00","id":951431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/951382-ephemeral-beings-influence-how-does-it-work?p=951407#post951407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you looked at the chart on pg. 256? Influence 1 can act like Perfecting, Compelling, Unveiling and Knowing</div> </div> </div> </div>Influence 1 actually doesn't seem to have much Compelling - that's only at Influence 2 (Manipulate). It doesn't really have Knowing or Veiling either, but that's mostly because Ephemerals have an instinctive awareness of their &quot;thing&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for the opposites, the chart doesn't list anything (probably because it would be counter productive in most cases), but you could easily rule that they <i>have</i> the inverse capabilities even if they don't use them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T19:31:35-07:00","id":951445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/951382-ephemeral-beings-influence-how-does-it-work?p=951418#post951418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes the chart is my mortal enemy :P<br /> It talk about what each dot of influence is capable of doing but doesn't really go into what it does mechanically speaking except for ephemeral conditions and resonance and giving Structure or Health equal to rank.<br /> How much defense can i get? What are the rules for playing with emotions? Can i switch out virtues? Give or add dots in skills? attributes? merits? etc? If a room is a bit cold , can i Control it with Cold Influence 3 to create an extreme environment? At what level? Can i give out Conditions to PCs or NPCs in their area of Influence? <br /> <br /> Like i get a general understanding of what you can do with the Influence, but how do I go from concept into mechanical effects without arbitrary pulling stuff ex rectum. <br /> <br /> Take for instance Strengthen, one use of it is to give someone under its purview extra Defense. There is a lot of difference between +1, +1 per success and + rank or anything else.<br /> <br /> I just have a problem going from abstracts to mechanics in this case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry to say, but the Influence mechanics are inherently abstract. You're going to have to get used to making judgment calls as ST if you want to use them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T19:45:42-07:00","id":951453,"title":"","content":"Yeah the problem is that it's inherently abstract and without any guidelines to use it. That's why i was looking here, if it was any consensus about the it in a mechanical sense or any good ideas to get some structure around it and lessen the arbitrary nature of it. Judgement calling works fine by why reinvent the wheel every time at the table, if there are good ideas to be used here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T20:43:23-07:00","id":951473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/951382-ephemeral-beings-influence-how-does-it-work?p=951418#post951418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much defense can i get? What are the rules for playing with emotions? Can i switch out virtues? Give or add dots in skills? attributes? merits? etc? If a room is a bit cold , can i Control it with Cold Influence 3 to create an extreme environment? At what level? Can i give out Conditions to PCs or NPCs in their area of Influence?</div> </div> </div> </div>A spirit might Influence an emotion tied with a character's Vice or Virtue to give it a full Willpower replenishment instead of a single dot, but I think such situations would be rare. You would only be adding dots in skills if said spirit was associated with that skill, like the God of Blades bestowing a Strengthen blessing on a swordsman. Attributes too. But at that point you have to deal with Duration if you don't want to get abstract with it.<br /> <br /> Similar to the Defense thing below I'd probably have changing it to an Extreme Environment be based on a number of successes, limited by Rank. A Rank 2 cold spirit isn't going to have the power to freeze an entire room.<br /> <br /> Giving out Conditions is probably a good way to represent certain Effects, since that's what Conditions are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Take for instance Strengthen, one use of it is to give someone under its purview extra Defense. There is a lot of difference between +1, +1 per success and + rank or anything else.<br /> <br /> I just have a problem going from abstracts to mechanics in this case. </div> </div> </div>I'd be tempted to let it add Successes to Defense to a max of spirit's Rank. Maybe more if there's an Exceptional Success or a Numina that allows one to spend extra Essence.<br /> <br /> For combat, you're going to be working more with Numina than Influences. But you can look at how they work, mechanically, to judge how you think Influences should.<br /> <br /> I checked in Mage, got the updated version and everything and it didn't really say that the different levels of Influence offer powers similar to the Arcana. But it's probably a good way to estimate whether something is doable or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-15-2016, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T22:06:00-07:00","id":951500,"title":"","content":"My recomendation is to treat Rank as a measure of the &quot;Primary Factor&quot; while leaving successes to determine the secondary ones. <br /> <br /> This means Streghten gives a bonus equal to Rank to whatever (successes) rolls fall under the Influence (for example, rolls to convince someone to adopt your beliefs for Indoctrination)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T22:40:44-07:00","id":956166,"title":"","content":"This is actually described a bit further on pg. 258. As total \u2022's of Influence == Rank, Rank is already a limiter. So let's take a G\u00f6etic demon (I'm old-school, and imo G\u00f6etia is the name of the practice, not the spirits it produces) with Rank 3 and Influence: Lust. The entity can Strengthen existing Lust for up to 1 hour/success, paying 1 or 2 Essence (depending on Duration desired), and rolling Power + Finesse vs. Resolve/Composure + Supernatural Tolerance. Success would open 1 Door of the target (or alternatively modify the subject's Impression upward by a stage per net success). However, this cannot induce Lust, only strengthen it where it already exists.<br /> <br /> This same entity could warp Love into carnal Lust (or change the target of the subject's existing Lust) for up to 10 mins/success for the cost of 2 Essence and by winning that same Contested roll, or change Fear into Lust for 1 min/success for 3 Essence by doing likewise. These effects would correspond to an Influence Condition and an Influence Tilt, respectively.<br /> <br /> Now let's turn this into a concrete example. A Guardian of the Veil needs to convince a mark to leave a party with her in order to take the mark's place at work tomorrow in a Seer-controlled company, but the subject's macho body-builder boyfriend is keeping everyone away from her. In order to keep her Signature from being read on the mark by the Seers, she decides to have her Lust demon help her out. Lust manifests as an extremely attractive woman who distracts the man, using an instance of it's Influence: Lust. The first usage is to Strengthen the lust that the macho body-builder naturally feels towards its Manifested form.<br /> <br /> The Mage capitalizes on the opportunity provided by the distraction to chat up the mark, who she knows from her recon previously had a serious relationship with her ex flat-mate. She commands Lust to use its Influence again, but this time to Manipulate the target of the mark's lust onto the Mage herself, and then to Strengthen that Lust to make her mundane efforts at picking up the mark easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1446,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1446-raikirah","user":"Raikirah","date":". 08-23-2016, 02:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1446-raikirah","name":"Raikirah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T16:21:36-07:00","id":958475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/951382-ephemeral-beings-influence-how-does-it-work?p=951473#post951473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I checked in Mage, got the updated version and everything ...</div> </div> </div> </div>What updated version is this? Where do I find it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T16:34:58-07:00","id":958484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RBAWintrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/951382-ephemeral-beings-influence-how-does-it-work?p=958475#post958475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What updated version is this? Where do I find it?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/181754/Mage-the-Awakening-2nd-Edition\" target=\"_blank\">It's just the most recent version.</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T07:47:27-07:00","id":959244,"title":"","content":"Ah thanks, I bought it a month ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}